cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or business, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Stark"
    given-names: "Tim Johann"
    alias: "timfromhcs"
title: "CQ-HECS: Classical Quantum High-Efficiency Compute Simulator & Four-Path Engine"
version: 5.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  CQ-HECS is a router-based classical simulator for quantum circuits with explicit
  capability contracts (stabilizer tableau, low-T branch sum, untruncated MPS, sparse-Pauli
  observables with a per-observable truncation bound), a typed result contract that keeps
  approximation, floating-point and sampling error apart, a sound SAT surface with checked
  certificates, local Studio/MCP/CLI/browser surfaces and a research evidence ledger. It is
  not a quantum computer, does not claim to resolve P versus NP, and its Quantum Gravity
  workbench studies finite models, not nature.
url: "https://github.com/timfromhcs/CQ-HECS"
keywords:
  - "quantum-simulation"
  - "vulkan-compute"
  - "spir-v"
  - "matrix-product-states"
  - "stabilizer-tableau"
  - "exact-ring-arithmetic"
  - "cryptanalysis"
  - "sat-solver"
  - "execution-planning"
  - "proof-checking"
